## Context

Built while working in Corporate Talent Acquisition Excellence and People Analytics at Cimory Group (2026). Weekly recruitment reporting across 5 business units (CORP, MP, MS, CMD, JESS) depended on combining separate tracking files kept by individual recruiters.

## Problem

Each recruiter and business unit maintained their own Excel workbook for manpower requests (FPTK) and candidate sourcing. Every week, roughly 17 files with mismatched header names, column orders, and date formats had to be merged and cleaned by hand before the weekly Board of Directors (BOD) presentation could be updated.

## My role

Owner: I designed the schema-driven mapping architecture, wrote the VBA compilation, validation, monitoring, and PowerPoint automation modules, and later evolved the solution into the web-based FPTK & Sourcing Database.

## As-is analysis

Manual weekly compilation required opening each recruiter file, fixing inconsistent headers and dates, checking duplicates and blacklist entries, recalculating funnel metrics, and copying charts and tables into PowerPoint slides under tight weekly deadlines.

## Requirements

- Compile FPTK, candidate sourcing, position codes, and candidate blacklist files from configured input folders into master sheets.
- Handle varying source column names and orders without breaking whenever a recruiter adjusts a template.
- Normalize names, dates, and codes while logging corrupted rows and duplicate entries.
- Generate monitoring, funneling, and recruiter performance views and update the weekly BOD PowerPoint deck automatically.

## Solution design

Instead of hardcoding column positions, I built a schema-driven header mapping sheet (`modSchemaAdjustment`, `frmHeaderAdjustment`) with 340+ field definitions and aliases so differently named or ordered columns map cleanly into one target layout with full schema-change logging.

## Build

Implemented modular Excel VBA workbooks covering compilation (`m02_MainCompiler`, `m11_DBSourcingCompiler`, `m06_CompileDBKodePosisi_FPTK`, `m10_CompileBlacklist`), data quality (`modLookup`, `modFPTKCompatibilityCleanup`), monitoring reports (`modMonitoring`, `modRecruiterMapping`), late-bound PowerPoint slide updates (`UpdatetoPPT`), and run controls with progress tracking, backups, archiving, and OneDrive export (`m15_ProgressManagement`, `m17_ExportAndBackup`, `modSaveToOneDrive`). Source code (template and VBA modules without candidate data): [github.com/thunderclouds863/recruitment-data-compiler-vba](https://github.com/thunderclouds863/recruitment-data-compiler-vba).

## Verification

Verified compiled master sheets, duplicate flags, funnel calculations, and generated PowerPoint slides against manual weekly reports across business units before rolling out for regular weekly reporting.

## Outcome

Automated about 60-70% of the weekly Board of Directors recruitment report, standardized ~17 recruiter files into one dataset, and established the business rules later migrated into the FPTK & Sourcing Database web application.

## Reflection

Building a schema-driven Excel VBA tool first delivered immediate weekly time savings inside the team's existing workflow while revealing the exact governance rules needed for the subsequent PostgreSQL web application.
